# Force LF line endings for all text files, in the repository AND on checkout,
# for EVERY platform. This is required for cross-platform build correctness.
#
# WHY: GitHub's `windows-latest` runner ships with `core.autocrlf=true`, so a
# fresh `actions/checkout` rewrites LF -> CRLF for text files on disk. Any file
# whose RAW BYTES are hashed at build time then hashes differently on Windows
# than on Linux. Concretely, `crates/maos-corpus-gen/build.rs` SHA256-pins the
# seed `*.toml` files (emitting `sha_check_{sr,rt,ccac}.rs`); the pins are the
# LF hashes, so a CRLF checkout fails the `windows-check` build only. The same
# trap applies to any other byte-hashed text fixture (corpora `*.jsonl`,
# manifests, include_str!/include_bytes! data).
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect binaries (files containing NUL bytes are
# left untouched); `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf` per-path so checkouts are
# LF everywhere. All tracked text in this repo is already LF, so enabling this
# produces no working-tree churn — it only pins the Windows-runner behaviour.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply any line-ending conversion (belt-and-braces over
# `text=auto`'s NUL-byte heuristic).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.tar   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
